docdb_family_id,sample,family_year,first_office,title_en,abstract_en,titles,is_relevant,is_relevant_broad,grey_zone,note
86409309,block6,2021,KR,APPARATUS AND SYSTEM FOR LAUNCHING AND RECOVERING OF UNDERWATER MOVING BODY,"According to various embodiments of the present invention, by providing an apparatus and system for launching and recovering of an underwater vehicle, fluid resistance in the underwater environment can be reduced and underwater vehicles of various shapes and characteristics can be launched or recovered. In addition, according to various embodiments of the present invention, by providing an apparatus and system for launching and recovering of an underwater vehicle, folding and unfolding operations are possible, so there is no disruption to the operation of the mother ship when not in use.",APPARATUS AND SYSTEM FOR LAUNCHING AND RECOVERING OF UNDERWATER MOVING BODY,0,1,crew not stated,can be used by underwater drones
66681137,block6,2018,KR,Driving direction control apparatus for underwater vehicle,"A driving direction control apparatus for an underwater moving body according to an adequate embodiment of the present invention comprises: a rudder structure having a first rudder one end of which is formed in a streamlined shape, and a second rudder coupled to the other end of the first rudder; and a direction control unit having a nozzle unit provided at the other end of the first rudder so as to be situated on the outside compared to the second rudder, and a valve unit configured so as to open and close a flow path connected to the nozzle unit.",Driving direction control apparatus for underwater vehicle,0,1,crew not stated,underwater vehicle
96627781,block6,2025,CN,Autonomous decision-making and cluster collaborative agent system in complex mariculture environment,"The invention, which belongs to the technical field of the marine industry, discloses an autonomous decision-making and cluster cooperation agent system in a complex mariculture environment, the autonomous decision-making and cluster cooperation agent system in the complex mariculture environment comprises a hardware group and a software group, the hardware group comprises a camera, a visual algorithm industrial personal computer, a propeller, a sensor and a battery; the software group is arranged in the visual algorithm industrial personal computer, and the software group comprises a precise tracking and optimized path planning module, an obstacle avoidance module, an underwater agent positioning module, a multi-agent cooperative control module, a formation control module, a data collection module, a cooperative combat module, a decision module, a detection module, a low-noise module and an autonomous decision module. Smooth communication and positioning between the underwater vehicles can be guaranteed, the stability, intelligence and autonomy of the system are high, the accuracy of the AUV during cluster decision making is guaranteed, and the decision making efficiency is effectively improved.",Autonomous decision-making and cluster collaborative agent system in complex mariculture environment,1,1,,multi agent auv
53389951,block6,2013,KR,UNDERWATER CLEANING ROBOT,"Disclosed is an underwater cleaning robot. According to an embodiment of the present invention, the underwater cleaning robot comprises: a frame; a cleaning unit installed on the frame and cleaning a work target surface under water; a driving unit and a steering unit installed on the frame to drive the frame to the work target surface; and a separation unit installed on the frame and having an expansion member of an elastic material which is expanded by supplied gas, pressurizes the work target surface, and ejects the frame.",UNDERWATER CLEANING ROBOT,1,1,,underwater robot
97935187,block6,2025,CN,Acousto-optic combined underwater target autonomous searching and positioning method,"The acousto-optic combined underwater target autonomous searching and positioning method comprises the following steps: establishing an underwater target searching platform based on an underwater unmanned vehicle; pre-establishing an underwater target detection model on the underwater target searching platform; inputting a given target type, a task area and a target quantity into a task decision system; the task decision-making system firstly identifies information transmitted from the sonar system; the task decision system identifies information transmitted from the optical camera system; the task decision-making system judges the suspicious target object; the underwater unmanned vehicle continues to search or return voyage on the given target type, task area and target number, or acousto-optic combination is carried out in a return voyage target detection mode, and sonar detection and optical detection are combined far and near, and large-range preliminary screening and approaching recognition confirmation are combined; the underwater target searching efficiency is improved, the detection and discovery capability is also improved, and the problems of low searching efficiency, difficult positioning and the like are solved.",Acousto-optic combined underwater target autonomous searching and positioning method,1,1,,underwater robot
82230581,block6,2022,CN,Control method of mobile multilayer marine environment profile monitoring system,"The invention discloses a control method of a mobile multilayer marine environment profile monitoring system, the monitoring system comprises a tugboat, a drag chain and an underwater vehicle, the drag chain is connected with the tugboat and the underwater vehicle, and the tugboat is provided with a drag chain retracting and releasing mechanism; at least three sensors are arranged on the drag chain, and power supply and data transmission are realized between the sensors and the drag chain in an electromagnetic coupling manner; the control method specifically comprises the following steps: step 1, laying the underwater vehicle and the drag chain; step 2, monitoring navigation states of the tugboat and the underwater vehicle; step 3, predicting the attitude of the drag chain; and 4, drag chain attitude control: solving to obtain the position of the underwater vehicle and the adjustment length of the drag chain, and further controlling the underwater vehicle to move.",Control method of mobile multilayer marine environment profile monitoring system,0,1,others,tugboat connected to underwater
40187103,block6,2008,CN,Deep sea mercury hydraulic system,"The invention discloses a deep-sea mercury hydraulic system, which is characterized by including a head mercury tank, an end mercury tank and a hydraulic oil tank. The upper parts and the lower parts of the head mercury tank and the end mercury tank respectively have hydraulic oil and mercury. The hydraulic oil tank is filled with hydraulic oil and is provided with a proportion valve, an oil pump, an electric motor and a safety valve; the oil inlet of the oil pump is communicated with the hydraulic oil in the hydraulic oil tank and the oil outlet of the oil pump is connected with a pressure port of the proportion valve. The oil return port of the proportion valve is communicated with the hydraulic oil in the hydraulic oil tank and the two outlets of the proportion valve are respectively communicated with the upper parts of the internal cavities of the head mercy tank and the end mercury tank by means of pipelines and the lower parts of the head mercury tank and the end mercury tank are communicated with each other by means of mercury pipes. The deep-sea mercury hydraulic system can not only prolong the service lives of the pump, the pipelines and the valves, but also can avoid the environmental pollution caused by the leakage of mercury, and is suitable for adjusting the head weight and end weight of underwater robots in deep-sea.",Deep sea mercury hydraulic system,1,1,,system for underwater robots
71787069,block6,2019,US,Polyphase contactless induction power transfer system for transferring electrical power across gap,"An inductive power transfer system is used for transferring electrical power across a gap, such as an air gap or a liquid gap, such as to unmanned autonomous vehicles (UAVs). The power transfer system is a polyphase system that creates a travelling magnetic field in the air or liquid gap, implementing a resonant electro-magnetic (EM) field to allow larger gap separations and less precise alignments. The power transfer system may have a polyphase dynamoelectric machine attached to primary mechanical-inertial storage device with multiple stator and rotor ports connected to a polyphase traveling-wave inductive power transmitter apparatus. The system may be of use in transferring power to underwater vehicles in a subsea salt water environment. Such a power transfer system may part of a larger system for underwater power transfer, for instance at depths of at least 10 km, and/or at distances of 1 to 50 km.",Polyphase contactless induction power transfer system for transferring electrical power across gap || ギャップを介して電力を伝達するための多相非接触誘導電力伝達システム || POLYPHASE CONTACTLESS INDUCTION POWER TRANSFER SYSTEM FOR TRANSFERRING ELECTRICAL POWER ACROSS GAP,0,1,generic ,underwater vehicle application
98198407,block6,2025,CN,Submarine cable information monitoring equipment,"The invention discloses submarine cable information monitoring equipment, and belongs to the technical field of cable protection monitoring, the submarine cable information monitoring equipment comprises an underwater robot, a folding and extending mechanism, a monitoring mechanism and a fixed point marking mechanism, the folding and extending mechanism for folding and extending is installed on the lower side of a shell of the underwater robot, and the monitoring mechanism is installed on the lower side of the shell of the underwater robot. The output end of the folding extension mechanism is provided with a monitoring mechanism for carrying out multi-process monitoring on the submarine cable, the output end of the folding extension mechanism is provided with a fixed point marking mechanism for carrying out clamping marking on the damaged part of the submarine cable, and the fixed point marking mechanism comprises a self-clamping marking assembly and a clamping moving assembly; and a plurality of self-clamping marking assemblies for providing positioning marks are mounted at the output end of the folding and extending mechanism. By means of the mode, rapid directional marking can be carried out on the part, needing to be overhauled, of the cable, follow-up workers can conveniently carry out overhauling according to marking points, and continuous comprehensive monitoring and evaluation of various sensors can be carried out along the submarine cable.",Submarine cable information monitoring equipment,1,1,,underwater robot monitoring
71332618,block6,2019,AU,An Unmanned Aerial Vehicle,"The present invention discloses an unmanned aerial vehicle, which includes a body provided with a plurality of flying propellers and buoyancy feet, and a retraction and pay-off device is also provided within the body or the underwater vehicle, which pulls back or releases the underwater vehicle by retracting or releasing the control cable; the underwater vehicle includes submarine propellers, a camera, and lights. The advantageous effects of the present invention are these: after the unmanned vehicle stops on the water surface, the underwater vehicle submerges the water through the wireless remote control, and the lights and the camera are turned on, and then the submarine propellers are driven to find the target objects for observation and recording. After recording, the remote cable control motor drives the cable control gear to retract the underwater vehicle, and finally the unmanned aerial vehicle flies back being controlled remotely. The control cable can also be used as a traction rope with low cost and strong practicability. Fig. 4 Fig. 5",An Unmanned Aerial Vehicle || An unmanned aerial vehicle,1,1,,underwater and surface fuctioning
94425565,block6,2024,CN,Robot stable tracking control method in large turbulent flow environment based on learning,"The invention belongs to the technical field of robots, and relates to a learning-based stable tracking control method for a robot in a large turbulent flow environment. According to the method, a learning-based stable control strategy is provided for uncertainty in the turbulent flow environment, structural transformation of the strategy is achieved through tolerance errors, and the adaptability of the robot in the complex and changeable turbulent flow environment is improved. Compared with the prior art, the robustness of the trajectory tracking control strategy of the underwater robot can be improved, and the practical engineering application value can be improved due to the combination of the strategy and the sensing data.",Robot stable tracking control method in large turbulent flow environment based on learning,1,1,,underwater application
94042039,block6,2024,CN,Low-cost reusable full-sea-depth equipment sacrificial anode and manufacturing method thereof,"The invention discloses an ocean engineering and underwater robot equipment technology, and aims to provide a low-cost reusable full-sea-depth equipment sacrificial anode and a manufacturing method thereof, the technical scheme is that the sacrificial anode comprises a sacrificial anode body, the sacrificial anode body comprises a shell made of a titanium alloy material, excellent corrosion resistance and structural strength are achieved, and the device is used for being installed on equipment; the zinc block serves as a sacrificial anode, is fixed in the shell and is used for being in contact with seawater to generate electrochemical reaction; the polyurethane adhesive is used for filling and controlling the corrosion sectional area of the zinc block and enhancing the stability of the whole structure; the device has the advantages of flexible installation design, adoption of low-cost materials, guarantee of structural stability and corrosion resistance, reusability, remarkable reduction of the maintenance cost, suitability for various marine equipment, simple and reasonable structure, convenience in manufacturing, simplicity and convenience in operation, avoidance of defects in the prior art, and suitability for popularization, implementation and application; the invention is suitable for the technical field of ocean engineering and underwater robot equipment.",Low-cost reusable full-sea-depth equipment sacrificial anode and manufacturing method thereof,0,1,,underwater application
54078451,block6,2015,CN,Underwater releasing device with two trigger modes of pure mechanical timing and pure mechanical depth setting,"The invention provides an underwater releasing device with two trigger modes of pure mechanical timing and pure mechanical depth setting. The underwater releasing device comprises a mechanical timing starting valve, a depth setting blasting mechanism and a releasing mechanism, wherein the mechanical timing starting valve consists of a timing mechanism, a linkage mechanism and a valve, and radial sealing is realized by a mechanical timing rotary button and a valve energy storing rotary button with an upper end cover through an O-shaped sealing ring; a timer shaft and a ball valve shaft are in the coaxially hinged connection design with a rotary button shaft, the timer shaft and the ball valve shaft are provided with gear rods, and the rotary button shaft is provided with a shifting rod; a timer cam is in contact with a linkage sliding shovel, a linkage lock tongue is in contact with a valve clamping disk, and energy is stored by the ball valve shaft through torsional springs; the opening of a ball valve is connected with an accommodating cavity of the releasing mechanism; a hole is formed in an upper cover of the depth setting blasting mechanism and communicated with outside, grease exists in an oil sac, and a blasting piece pressure relief opening is communicated with the accommodating cavity of the releasing mechanism; a steel ball is blocked by the releasing mechanism, so that the steel ball is prevented from rolling inwards, and an inner cylinder body is prevented from falling downwards. The underwater releasing device disclosed by the invention has the two trigger modes and can be used for underwater robots, underwater engineering machinery, underwater engineering equipment and the like.",Underwater releasing device with two trigger modes of pure mechanical timing and pure mechanical depth setting,0,1,,underwater application
97851158,block6,2025,CN,Underwater unmanned vehicle based on photo-thermal cooperative power generation,"The underwater unmanned vehicle comprises a main body and a power generation system, and the power generation system comprises a curved surface photovoltaic power generation unit, a phase change heat storage thermoelectric power generation unit and an intelligent cooperative control unit. The curved-surface photovoltaic power generation unit and the phase-change heat-storage thermoelectric power generation unit are attached to the outer surface of the main body, and the curved-surface photovoltaic power generation unit and the phase-change heat-storage thermoelectric power generation unit wrap the main body through a first attaching face and a second attaching face respectively. The curved surface photovoltaic power generation unit and the phase change heat storage thermoelectric power generation unit are electrically connected with a propeller of the main body respectively; the intelligent cooperative control unit is in signal connection with the curved surface photovoltaic power generation unit and the phase change heat storage thermoelectric power generation unit.",Underwater unmanned vehicle based on photo-thermal cooperative power generation,1,1,,uuv
55199180,block6,2014,CN,Special thin optical cable,"The invention relates to a special thin optical cable which is characterized in that the special thin optical cable comprises an outer sheath layer, an optical fiber, aramid fiber reinforcers and an adhesive. The external diameter of the outer sheath layer is not larger than 2 mm; the optical fiber is arranged inside the outer sheath layer; the plurality of aramid fiber reinforcers are filled between the outer sheath layer and the optical fiber; the plurality of aramid fiber reinforcers are in uniform arrangement; the adhesive is filled among the plurality of aramid fiber reinforcers and enables the plurality of aramid fiber reinforcers to be fixed and combined together; the aramid fiber reinforcer is a PBO fiber reinforcer, a glass fibre reinforcer or a carbon fiber reinforcer; and the adhesive is an epoxy resin adhesive, an epoxy acrylic adhesive, a polyurethane adhesive or a UV-curing adhesive. The special thin optical cable is simple in structure, reasonable in design and good in use effect, solves the problems that the cable cannot well meet the requirements of underwater robots and fiber guided weapons and the like at present, and meanwhile, is light in weight, and high in tensile strength.",Special thin optical cable,0,1,,underwater drones usage
58457348,block6,2015,RU,"TOWED UNDERWATER VEHICLE, EQUIPPED WITH SONAR EQUIPMENT FOR DETECTING SILTING FACILITIES AND PIPELINES, AND THEIR SUBSEQUENT MONITORING","FIELD: shipbuilding.SUBSTANCE: invention relates to the production of underwater operations to probe the seabed, pipeline routes with geo-referenced detection silted objects. Towed underwater vehicle (TUV) is designed as a hollow cylindrical body with a removable head and the tail stabilizer, equipped with a device deepens and computationally-control module and connected to the ship-towing cable-rope. Sonar equipment includes a parametric profiler, consisting of an antenna radiating parametric pumping and receiving antenna, means of processing and recording of sonar signals. TUV further comprises an active sonar, n number of uninhabited small self-propelled platforms located aft of the TUV and equipped with a propulsion system, automatic traffic control system, ballast-equalization system, chassis, magnetometric flaw, an identifier of explosives, poisonous and radioactive substances, a small-sized underwater television apparatus. The vessel is equipped with a towing-control system pits small-sized self-propelled platform.EFFECT: invention provides the detection of underwater objects by providing access to hard to reach items, surveyed underwater objects and enhanced functionality.","TOWED UNDERWATER VEHICLE, EQUIPPED WITH SONAR EQUIPMENT FOR DETECTING SILTING FACILITIES AND PIPELINES, AND THEIR SUBSEQUENT MONITORING",1,1,,underwater vehicle
82533701,block6,2022,CN,Wearable underwater exoskeleton robot for rehabilitation and use method thereof,"The invention provides a wearable underwater exoskeleton robot for rehabilitation and a using method thereof, and belongs to the technical field of artificial intelligence. The wearable underwater exoskeleton robot comprises a basic device, and a sensing mechanism, a control mechanism, a driving mechanism and an executing mechanism are arranged on the basic device; the sensing mechanism is in electric signal connection with the control mechanism, the control mechanism receives and processes motion data sent by the sensing mechanism and sends the motion data to the driving mechanism, the control mechanism is in electric signal connection with the driving mechanism, the driving mechanism is in electric signal connection with the executing mechanism, and the driving mechanism drives the executing mechanism to move; the basic device comprises a waist fastening piece and leg fastening pieces, and the waist fastening piece and the leg fastening pieces are arranged on the human body in an attached mode; the executing mechanism comprises a waist exoskeleton, a leg exoskeleton and an underwater propeller, the waist exoskeleton is arranged on the waist fastening piece, the leg exoskeleton is arranged on the leg fastening piece, and the underwater propeller conducts propelling in the advancing direction of the human body. The rehabilitation training of the patient is facilitated, and the rehabilitation efficiency of the patient is improved.",Wearable underwater exoskeleton robot for rehabilitation and use method thereof,0,0,,irrelevant 
90888191,block6,2022,CN,Filling device for building underwater defects,"The invention belongs to the technical field of filling equipment, and particularly relates to a filling device for building underwater defects, which comprises at least one material storage cavity I, at least one material storage cavity II, a driver, a static mixer and a material injection assembly, and is characterized in that the material storage cavity I and the material storage cavity II are respectively provided with a piston rod I and a piston rod II; the driver drives the piston rod I and the piston rod II to synchronously move; the filling device is carried to an underwater defect part of a building by an underwater robot, so that the filling device is not easily limited by water depth and directly reaches the defect part, the distance for conveying a filling agent is greatly shortened, and the filling agent can be used for filling the underwater defect part of the building. The device can also adapt to various and complex working surfaces; the filling agent can be accurately prepared according to the size of the underwater defect of the building, waste is avoided, and the extrusion speed of the filling agent is controlled through the driver so as to adapt to the defects of different depths and widths.",Filling device for building underwater defects,0,1,generic ,subsea equipment
95393521,block6,2024,CN,Vision-based underwater floating robot auxiliary motion control method,"The invention belongs to the technical field of motion control, and particularly relates to an underwater floating robot auxiliary motion control method based on vision. Comprising the following steps: step 1, calibrating an image coordinate system and a course; step 2, object identification and operation track generation; step 3, course control; and step 4, fixed-point hovering. The method has the beneficial effects that (1) only a monocular uncalibrated camera is adopted, and the course and the position of the floating robot are controlled by identifying repeated targets in a scene; (2) a deep learning method is adopted, a detection model is trained based on a data generation mode through a small number of field images, and meanwhile, a course planning map is generated based on a template image according to a detection result; and (3) realizing closed-loop control of real-time course and position by combining real-time target detection based on the track planning map and odometer information.",Vision-based underwater floating robot auxiliary motion control method,1,1,,underwater robot method 
77789595,block6,2021,CN,Lightweight underwater target detection method based on depth separable cavity convolution,"The invention provides a lightweight underwater target detection method based on depth separable cavity convolution. The method comprises the steps: employing an underwater robot to shoot an underwater target image, obtaining an underwater target detection data set, carrying out the improvement of a VGG16-based Faster R-CNN model, reading the underwater target detection data set, carrying out the training and testing of the improved model, and carrying out the detection of an underwater target; and carrying the detection model and the trained detection model weight on an underwater robot platform, carrying out real-time detection on an underwater image, and identifying an underwater target. According to the method, the resolution of the feature map is increased, the method is suitable for multi-scale targets, and the parameter quantity in the detection process is reduced by reducing the number of channels of the feature map and compressing the full-connection layer, so that the target recognition speed is increased, and the network has the lightweight characteristic, can be carried on an underwater robot platform and has a wide application prospect.",Lightweight underwater target detection method based on depth separable cavity convolution,1,1,,underwater application
55651256,block6,2014,KR,CLEANING ROBOT FOR UNDERWATER USE,"The present invention relates to an underwater cleaning robot which stabilizes traveling on foreign substances, such as underwater sludge, and removes a large amount of foreign substances. The underwater cleaning robot comprises: a robot body; a traveling unit which is arranged in the robot body to move the robot body; and a foreign substance removal unit which is arranged in the robot body to remove the foreign substances and is moved in a height direction by corresponding to the height of the foreign substances. Therefore, the present invention widens a cleaning area and improves cleaning efficiency as the foreign substance removal unit can grind and remove frontward foreign substances piled up high.",CLEANING ROBOT FOR UNDERWATER USE,1,1,,underwater robot
96682899,block6,2025,CN,Equivalent hydrodynamic load lateral loading test device and test process thereof,"The equivalent hydrodynamic load lateral loading test device comprises a triangular reaction frame fixed on a foundation, a model connecting plate is mounted on the triangular reaction frame through a fastener, a test element is fixedly mounted on the triangular reaction frame through a constraint transition section, a loading transition section is mounted at the head of the test element and is hinged to a loading cross beam through a loading shaft, and the loading cross beam is hinged to the model connecting plate. The loading cross beam penetrates through a cavity in the upper part of the supporting vertical beam, and a loading concave spherical surface is fixed at the head part of the loading cross beam; the device further comprises a transverse reaction frame, a hydraulic actuator is installed on the end face of the transverse reaction frame through an oil cylinder connecting plate, a loading convex spherical surface matched with the loading concave spherical surface is fixed to the output end of the hydraulic actuator, and the hydraulic actuator is connected with an electro-hydraulic servo loading control system to achieve equivalent loading of the hydrodynamic load. The strain and deformation response of the stern structure of the underwater vehicle under the equivalent load is obtained, and the reliability of a numerical simulation result and the feasibility of a load equivalent method can be verified by comparing the strain and deformation response with a simulation result.",Equivalent hydrodynamic load lateral loading test device and test process thereof,0,1,,underwater-vehicle engineering
68847522,block6,2018,KR,Hopping-frequency coding based transmission and reception method and apparatus to estimate the information of a high-speed underwater vehicle in short range,"The present invention relates to a method for transmitting and receiving a hopping frequency based on coding, and to an apparatus thereof. According to one embodiment of the present invention, the method for transmitting and receiving a hopping frequency based on coding in an active sonar system comprises the steps of: transmitting a continuous wave signal hopping at least three frequency bands at a period shorter than the delay time of a reflected signal in a transmitter; and obtaining a frequency, a hopping time point, and a hopping frequency of a received signal from a receiver, and estimating a distance of a target and a Doppler frequency from the obtained frequency, the obtained hopping time point, and the obtained hopping frequency.",Hopping-frequency coding based transmission and reception method and apparatus to estimate the information of a high-speed underwater vehicle in short range,0,1,crew not stated,underwater vehicle
96504685,block6,2025,CN,Magnetic adsorption mobile underwater cleaning detection robot,"The invention provides a magnetic adsorption mobile underwater cleaning detection robot, and belongs to the technical field of underwater cleaning detection. Comprising a vehicle body frame, a damping mechanism, a power mechanism, a mounting base, a swing mechanism, a high-pressure water pipe, an adjusting mechanism and a cleaning mechanism; the vehicle body frame is provided with an electronic cabin; four groups of damping mechanisms are arranged; four groups of power mechanisms are arranged and are connected with the vehicle body frame through the damping mechanism; the mounting seat is arranged on the vehicle body frame; the swing mechanism is arranged in the mounting seat; the high-pressure water pipe is rotationally connected with the mounting disc; the adjusting mechanism is arranged on the mounting disc; and the cleaning mechanism is arranged on the high-pressure water pipe. Through cooperative arrangement of the swing mechanism, the cleaning mechanism and the high-pressure water gun, the high-pressure water gun swings to wash and clean the jacket structure or the bottom of the ship body, meanwhile, the cleaning mechanism works to scrub the jacket structure or the bottom of the ship body, and the cleaning quality and cleaning efficiency of the jacket structure or the bottom of the ship body are improved.",Magnetic adsorption mobile underwater cleaning detection robot,1,1,,underwater robot
53115074,block6,2015,CN,Image recognition based underwater welding robot,"The invention relates to an image recognition based underwater welding robot which comprises welding gun driving equipment, a high-definition image sensor, an image processor and a master controller, wherein the high-definition image sensor is used for acquiring a welding image of a welded workpiece; the image processor is connected with the high-definition image sensor to carry out image recognition treatment on the welding image so as to detect the position of welding in the welding image; and the master controller is connected with the welding gun driving equipment and the image processor to control the welding gun driving equipment based on the position of welding to drive an underwater welding gun to reach the position of welding. According to the invention, intelligent degree of the underwater welding robot can be increased, and positioning and welding of an underwater welding seam can be finished without manual operation.",Image recognition based underwater welding robot || Underwater welding robot based on image identification,1,1,,underwater robot
96271648,block6,2025,CN,Ocean induced polarization and natural potential combined acquisition device and data processing method,"The invention discloses an ocean induced polarization and natural potential combined acquisition device and a data processing method, and solves the technical problem that the sulfide ore form cannot be accurately represented in the prior art. The system comprises a first underwater autonomous robot and a second underwater autonomous robot, the first underwater autonomous robot is provided with an induced polarization emission device, and the second underwater autonomous robot is provided with a natural potential acquisition device; the induced polarization emission device comprises an induced polarization control bin, a first watertight cable, an emission end positive pole and an emission end negative pole, and the natural potential acquisition equipment comprises a natural potential acquisition bin, a second watertight cable and a plurality of pairs of Ag/AgCl non-polarized electrodes. According to the method, the distribution characteristics of submarine sulfides can be more accurately explained, the multiplicity of solutions is reduced, and the exploration accuracy and reliability are improved.",Ocean induced polarization and natural potential combined acquisition device and data processing method,,,,
76716572,block6,2021,CN,Automatic homeward voyage method and device for underwater autonomous navigation robot,"The invention provides an automatic homeward voyage method and device for an underwater autonomous navigation robot. The method comprises the following steps of carrying out the map creation and positioning of a surrounding environment through a position sensor after the underwater autonomous navigation robot completes the task execution, establishing a corresponding grid map, performing dilation operation on a plurality of obstacles in the grid map to generate a path of a grid Dirichlet graph forming a return path, and then performing path vectorization and topologization to obtain a topological path network, performing path planning by adopting a Dijkstra algorithm, and selecting an optimal return path, and performing real-time marine environment benchmark test on the data by adopting an artificial path planning algorithm, if the data is valid, adopting the optimal return path, and if the data is invalid, repeating the steps from the step of establishing the grid map. According to the method, a Dijkstra algorithm similar to a natural language is adopted for path planning, and data uncertainty and inaccuracy can be well processed.",Automatic homeward voyage method and device for underwater autonomous navigation robot,,,,
59199769,block6,2015,CN,Defense penetration path planing method of underwater vehicle,"The invention relates to a defense penetration path planing method of an underwater vehicle. The method is characterized by comprising the following steps of: performing discretization on a space by initializing parameters; generating a novel path by using an initialized harmony memory library; updating the harmony memory library; comparing and judging whether the finish condition is met or not; and if so, outputting the optimum path; and otherwise, returning the third step to further execute. By planing the path by means of a harmony search method (Harmony Search, HS), a method of only discretizing the defense penetration space in one-dimension when the whole defense penetration space is discretized while other dimensions are not changed. Here, x periphery is discretized, so that the whole space is divided into several planes which are parallel to a plane yOz, and therefore, a point is taken in each plane in the middle, and the starting point and the ending point are connected to form a path. On this basis, the starting point and the ending point are immobilized, and only the points selected from the plane in the middle can freely move in the corresponding plan. The full posture algorithm provided by the invention effectively solves the problem of erroneous judgment and overflow in a calculating process of a posture angle.",Defense penetration path planing method of underwater vehicle,,,,
98000996,block6,2025,CN,Underwater static sensing model construction method based on terrain fine grid division,"The invention discloses an underwater static perception model construction method based on terrain fine grid division, and belongs to the field of underwater visual perception. Fine grid division is performed on underwater topographic data, and the underwater vehicle is mapped to a corresponding grid position through a position, so that a static sensing model is constructed. Combining the surrounding environment of the lake, the terrain of the bottom of the lake and the safe navigation depth to construct a near non-safe area grid set, calculating a grid where the underwater vehicle is located in the future in real time, and giving an alarm if there is an intersection with the non-safe area grid set. The model can accurately sense the underwater static environment and guarantee the safe operation of the underwater vehicle.",Underwater static sensing model construction method based on terrain fine grid division,,,,
83163594,block6,2022,CN,Dynamic docking and recycling device of underwater vehicle with variable structure,"The invention discloses an underwater vehicle dynamic docking recovery device with a variable structure, and belongs to the technical field of underwater docking. Comprising a head butt joint device and a tail butt joint device which are installed on the head and the tail of an underwater vehicle respectively and used for dynamic end-to-end butt joint recovery between the underwater vehicles. The tail butt-joint device comprises a tail butt-joint external member, a butt-joint petal, an opening and closing mechanism and a fixing device; the bottom end of the tail butt joint kit is fixedly connected with the tail of the underwater vehicle, and a butt joint petal, an opening and closing mechanism and a fixing device are installed at the top end of the tail butt joint kit. Opening and closing actions of the butt joint petals are controlled through the opening and closing mechanism, and butt joint with the head butt joint device is achieved. Fixed connection after butt joint is achieved through the fixing device; the bottom end of the head butt-joint device is fixedly connected with the head of the underwater vehicle, and the top end of the head butt-joint device is of a butt-joint structure installed with the butt-joint petals in a matched mode. According to the invention, dynamic docking between two underwater vehicles can be realized, and the docking vehicle can be effectively prevented from falling off.",Dynamic docking and recycling device of underwater vehicle with variable structure,,,,
41072476,block6,2008,JP,UNDERWATER CLEANING ROBOT AND AUXILIARY CLEANING WORK MACHINE,"<P>PROBLEM TO BE SOLVED: To improve the cleaning efficiency of an object to be cleaned by enlarging the cleaning surface of an underwater cleaning robot. <P>SOLUTION: The underwater cleaning robot is provided with a robot body 2 moving along the surface of the object to be cleaned which is present in the underwater and a cleaning nozzle unit 3 for cleaning the object to be cleaned by jetting high pressure water toward the surface of the object to be cleaned. An auxiliary cleaning work machine 70 is mounted inside the robot body and is provided with: a rotary shaft 76 provided rotatably in a work machine body 71; a cleaning nozzle unit 72 which is provided on the lower part of the rotary shaft, jets the high pressure water to the surface of the object to be cleaned and integrally rotates with the rotary shaft by the reaction force of jetting of the high pressure water to the surface of the object to be cleaned; and a propeller 73 which is provided on the upper part of the rotary shaft and rotates with the rotation of the rotary shaft to generate a force for pressing the work machine body to the surface of the object to be cleaned. <P>COPYRIGHT: (C)2009,JPO&INPIT",UNDERWATER CLEANING ROBOT AND AUXILIARY CLEANING WORK MACHINE,,,,
61936442,block6,2017,CN,"Remote controller testing method, apparatus and testing terminal thereof","The invention provides a remote controller testing method, an apparatus and a testing terminal thereof, which belong to the technical field of tests. The method is executed by the testing terminal. The method comprises the following steps: when connection is established with a to-be-measured remote controller, test operation on the to-be-measured remote controller carried out by users is monitored, a test feedback result corresponding to the test operation output by the to-be-measured remote controller is obtained, and the test feedback result is displayed on a test interface. The test operation can be carried out on the to-be-measured remote controller by the users, the test feedback result of the to-be-measured remote controller can be accurately obtained through the testing terminal, artificial intuition is not required for simple evaluation on the remote controller, reliability is high, and the testing terminal can be better used for the remote controllers with complex structure and high requirement on test results such as underwater robots and unmanned planes.","Remote controller testing method, apparatus and testing terminal thereof",,,,
95024984,block6,2024,FR,"AUTONOMOUS NAVIGATION SYSTEM FOR AN UNDERWATER VEHICLE, NAVIGATION ASSEMBLY AND NAVIGATION METHOD IMPLEMENTED BY SUCH A SYSTEM","The invention relates to a navigation system (100) for an underwater vehicle, which system comprises: - a data acquisition module (200) for collecting data from sensors of said vehicle and from a surface unit; - a fusion module (300) for retrieving a part of said collected data, which module comprises a processing algorithm for discriminating the retrieved data and for determining a position of the vehicle; - a movement module (400) for calculating the difference between the determined position and a setpoint position and for sending an order of movement to the vehicle when the difference between the determined position and the setpoint position exceeds a threshold value; - a monitoring module (500) for ensuring that the order of movement sent is coherent.","Système de navigation autonome d’un véhicule sous-marin, ensemble de navigation et procédé de navigation mis en œuvre par un tel système || AUTONOMOUS NAVIGATION SYSTEM FOR AN UNDERWATER VEHICLE, NAVIGATION ASSEMBLY AND NAVIGATION METHOD IMPLEMENTED BY SUCH A SYSTEM",,,,
98238293,block6,2025,CN,Underwater image enhancement method based on multiple attention mechanisms,"The invention provides an underwater image enhancement method based on multiple attention mechanisms, and belongs to the technical field of underwater image enhancement. The method comprises the following steps: 1, dividing an underwater image data set to obtain a training set, a verification set and a test set; 2, training an underwater image enhancement network by using the constructed underwater image data set to obtain a trained network model; and 3, deploying the trained network model to an underwater robot for application, performing enhancement processing on the obtained underwater image, and providing the enhanced image to observation equipment. According to the method, the visual effect of the underwater image can be remarkably improved, and the problem of poor underwater image quality caused by light scattering and attenuation and uneven illumination in the underwater environment is solved.",Underwater image enhancement method based on multiple attention mechanisms,,,,
99237247,block6,2025,CN,Sea-land-air-diving integrated inspection scheduling method,"The invention discloses a sea-land-air-diving integrated inspection scheduling method, relates to the technical field of electrical equipment inspection, and solves the problem that the prior art is lack of collaborative assessment of multi-dimensional dynamic risks and cross-domain integrated scheduling optimization capability. Through fusion of multi-source heterogeneous data, risk quantitative prediction transition from single experience judgment to data driving is realized, and composite risk levels of sea-land-air-dive domains in future time periods can be actively identified and evaluated instead of passive response. In addition, an economic, time, energy consumption and risk avoidance four-dimensional weighting objective function is also established, a unified collaborative scheduling language and optimization criterion are provided for heterogeneous inspection equipment, and an unmanned aerial vehicle, an unmanned ship, an underwater robot and the like are converted into a global linkage organic whole from an isolated operation unit. The model not only can dynamically adjust the inspection strategy according to the real-time environment change to realize the balance between the safety risk and the resource efficiency, but also can improve the prediction precision by continuously iterating historical data.",Sea-land-air-diving integrated inspection scheduling method,,,,
86931459,block6,2023,CN,Brain-controlled underwater vehicle system based on motor imagery and control method thereof,"The invention discloses a brain-controlled underwater vehicle system based on motor imagery and a control method thereof. The brain-controlled underwater vehicle system comprises an electroencephalogram acquisition subsystem, an electroencephalogram analysis subsystem, a control decision subsystem, a brain-controlled underwater vehicle and a sensing subsystem, the electroencephalogram acquisition subsystem is used for acquiring and transmitting electroencephalogram signals to the electroencephalogram analysis subsystem; the electroencephalogram analysis subsystem is used for carrying out preprocessing, feature extraction and mode classification on the electroencephalogram signals and sending a brain control instruction to the control decision subsystem; the sensing subsystem is used for sensing information of the sensing subsystem and feeding back the information to the control decision subsystem; and the control decision subsystem is used for judging the brain control instruction according to the information of the sensing subsystem, converting the brain control instruction into a motion control signal and sending the motion control signal to the brain control underwater vehicle.",Brain-controlled underwater vehicle system based on motor imagery and control method thereof,,,,
90593661,block6,2023,CN,Control method of underwater vehicle and underwater navigation system,"The invention discloses a control method of an underwater vehicle and an underwater navigation system, and relates to the technical field of underwater navigation, the underwater navigation system comprises a control module, a wearable device, an underwater vehicle and an interactive sensing module, a plane image acquired by an image acquisition module in the underwater vehicle is acquired, and the plane image is displayed on the wearable device; processing the plane image to determine a three-dimensional image, controlling a display module in the wearable device to display the three-dimensional image, and determining a motion control parameter according to motion capture data sent by the interactive sensing module to control the underwater vehicle to execute a motion corresponding to the motion control parameter, the motion capture data is data which is captured by the interactive perception module and corresponds to a control scheme determined by an operator according to the three-dimensional image. According to the scheme provided by the invention, the underwater vehicle can be visually and efficiently controlled at the first visual angle, the control difficulty of the underwater vehicle is reduced, the operation is simple, the training threshold of operators is reduced, and practical application is facilitated.",Control method of underwater vehicle and underwater navigation system,,,,
98084920,block6,2025,CN,Water bloom intelligent prediction and early warning system and method based on AI large model,"The invention discloses an intelligent water bloom prediction and early warning system and method based on an AI large model. The system is mainly composed of a data acquisition module, a data preprocessing module, an AI large model module, an early warning module and a visualization module. The data acquisition module is responsible for widely collecting multi-source data of a target water area. A water quality sensor, an underwater robot and other equipment go deep into a water body to accurately collect physical and chemical parameters of the water body, a meteorological station is utilized to obtain comprehensive meteorological data in real time, hydrological data is obtained from a water conservancy department database or on-site hydrological monitoring equipment, and satellite remote sensing data is obtained by means of a satellite receiving station or a third-party remote sensing data platform. Macroscopic information such as water color, chlorophyll a concentration distribution and water area change is covered. The invention belongs to the field of water environment monitoring and early warning, and particularly relates to an intelligent water bloom predicting and early warning system and method based on an AI large model.",Water bloom intelligent prediction and early warning system and method based on AI large model,,,,
65850435,block6,2018,CN,Improved RRT-based underwater vehicle rolling planning algorithm capable of effectively improving search efficiency,"The invention relates to the technical field of path planning, in particular to an improved RRT-based underwater vehicle rolling planning algorithm capable of effectively improving search efficiency.Compared with a basic RRT algorithm, the improved RRT algorithm utilizes node visibility to obtain a node extension direction and the node extension step length through 2-layer selection, the simulation experiment shows that the algorithm is higher in the search efficiency compared to the rolling planning based on the basic RRT, searches the improved RRT algorithm and the basic RRT algorithm in aplurality of complex environments, the experiment data shows that the improved RRT algorithm is less in the search time in the complex environments and fewer in the corresponding node quantity compared to the RRT algorithm.",Improved RRT-based underwater vehicle rolling planning algorithm capable of effectively improving search efficiency,,,,
93902581,block6,2024,CN,Illuminating device of aircraft,"The invention discloses a lighting device of an underwater vehicle, and belongs to the technical field of underwater vehicle accessories. A protective shell is arranged on the outer layer of a lamp body to protect the lamp body, the protective shell is provided with a glass cover for a light source of the lamp body to emit light, a movable piston is arranged, and after the lighting device sinks into water along with the underwater vehicle, the piston is pressed by water pressure, so that the lamp body is protected; a piston is arranged in the protective shell, the inner space of the protective shell is reduced, the difference between the inner pressure intensity and the outer water pressure of the protective shell is reduced, the front baffle ring and the rear baffle ring limit the moving curve of the piston, the front baffle ring separates a containing space for the lamp body, and the rear baffle ring blocks the piston so that the piston can be prevented from sliding out of the shell barrel. The light body is protected from being damaged in the underwater navigation process, and the variable-pressure protection shell is arranged, so that the protection shell is prevented from being damaged due to too large water pressure when the protection shell dives into a deep water area.",Illuminating device of aircraft,,,,
94339759,block6,2024,CN,Magnetic coupling communication circuit design method,"The invention discloses a magnetic coupling communication circuit design method, and belongs to the field of wireless charging, and the method comprises the following steps: obtaining electromagnetic simulation parameters based on the diameter of an underwater vehicle and the axial distance of a charging cabin; calculating the compensation inductance and capacitance value of the primary side and the capacitance value of the secondary side based on the electromagnetic simulation parameters to obtain compensation parameters; obtaining an optimal information transient response adjusting resistance based on the electromagnetic simulation parameters and the compensation parameters; and obtaining the optimal signal-to-noise ratio and the optimal information transmission gain of the communication circuit based on the optimal information transient response adjusting resistance and circuit parameters. According to the invention, the value of the information receiving resistor can be reasonably adjusted, so that the system has high signal-to-noise ratio and information transmission gain, and the information error rate is effectively reduced.",Magnetic coupling communication circuit design method,,,,
98470935,block6,2025,CN,Underwater target detection device and method based on binocular fusion line structured light,"The invention relates to the technical field of underwater target detection, and discloses an underwater target detection device and method based on binocular fusion line structured light, the device comprises a binocular structured light system and an information processing unit which are installed at the bow of an underwater robot, and the binocular structured light system is in communication connection with the information processing unit; the binocular structured light system comprises vertically arranged array laser and an underwater binocular camera, and the array laser is used for projecting line structured light stripes to an underwater target and forming a structured light image on the surface of the target; the underwater binocular camera is used for capturing a structured light image and sending the structured light image to the information processing unit; and the information processing unit is used for performing edge detection on the received structured light image to obtain line structured light projection stripes of the target surface, and further obtaining three-dimensional point cloud coordinates of the target surface. According to the invention, an underwater three-dimensional space can be fully covered, and three-dimensional perception and accurate identification of underwater suspended and semi-buried targets can be realized.",Underwater target detection device and method based on binocular fusion line structured light,,,,
67010176,block6,2019,CN,Underwater vehicle pressure-resisting housing self-reinforcing method,"An underground vehicle pressure-resisting housing self-reinforcing method relates to the technical field of marine equipment. The underwater vehicle pressure-resisting housing self-reinforcing methodcomprises the following operation steps of: selecting a material model; analyzing the strength of a cylindrical rib-equipped structure and a cylindrical no-rib structure of a traditional cylindrical pressure-resisting housing structure; according to the definition of a residual stress in material mechanics, deriving the distribution rule of a residual stress of a cylinder with plastic deformationin a wall thickness direction; deriving a relation between an interference amount of a punch and the radius of a plastic interface; obtaining an optimal yield radius, and when an outer pressure is bear and the cylinder is in a full yield state, deriving a pressure bearing capability theoretical improvement value after self-reinforcing processing, and an axial stress which is generated on the cylinder wall at the radius in the function of the outer pressure. The underground vehicle pressure-resisting housing self-reinforcing method has advantages of greatly improving pressure resistance of theunderwater vehicle based on an original structure, and realizing high stable performance and higher practicability.",Underwater vehicle pressure-resisting housing self-reinforcing method,,,,
91393158,block6,2024,CN,Pressure-resistant underwater vehicle shell based on acoustic black hole principle,"The invention discloses a pressure-resistant underwater vehicle shell based on the acoustic black hole principle. The pressure-resistant underwater vehicle shell comprises an underwater vehicle shell body and a plurality of annular reinforcing ribs connected to the inner wall and the outer wall of the underwater vehicle shell body. A plurality of single-blade acoustic black hole components are annularly and symmetrically distributed on the two sides of the inner and outer wall annular reinforcing ribs; a plurality of double-blade acoustic black hole components are annularly distributed between the single-blade acoustic black hole components; damping layers are attached to the lower surfaces of the single-blade acoustic black hole components and the double-blade acoustic black hole components; the upper surface of the single-blade acoustic black hole component is a streamline tapered surface along one side; the middle of the double-blade acoustic black hole component is a table-shaped protrusion, and the two sides of the double-blade acoustic black hole component are symmetrical streamline tapered faces. The multiple annular reinforcing ribs are connected to the shell so that the compression strength of the shell in underwater navigation can be effectively improved, the multiple single-blade and double-blade acoustic black hole components are arranged, vibration bending wave energy is concentrated to the acoustic black hole area to achieve energy absorption and dissipation, and the high-efficiency vibration and noise reduction performance advantage is achieved.",Pressure-resistant underwater vehicle shell based on acoustic black hole principle,,,,
76813315,block6,2021,CN,Landslide safety monitoring device based on underwater diving and shooting equipment and positioning method,"Disclosed in the present disclosure is a landslide safety monitoring apparatus based on an underwater photographing deVice. The landslide safety monitoring apparatus includes: an underwater robot, a water surface unmanned mother ship and a ground control center room; the water surface unmanned mother ship is connected to the underwater robot by means of a first wireless communication line; and the water surface unmanned mother ship is connected to the ground control center room by means of a second wireless communication line. Integration of signal acquisition, processing analysis and wireless transmission requirements of monitoring information and environment data of deformation of an underwater landslide is achieved by taking a shipborne underwater robot as a core, combining underwater sonar and underwater binocular imaging positioning technologies and using a wireless control and communication transmission system.",Landslide safety monitoring device based on underwater diving and shooting equipment and positioning method || LANDSLIDE SAFETY MONITORING APPARATUS BASED ON UNDERWATER PHOTOGRAPHING DEVICE AND POSITIONING METHOD,,,,
46717496,block6,2012,KR,METHOD FOR ESTIMATING PASSIVE SONAR DATA OF UNDERWATER VEHICLE FOR REAL-TIME SIMULATION AND SIMULATING APPARATUS HAVING THE SAME,PURPOSE: A passive sonar information method of an underwater moving object and a simulation apparatus including the same are provided to easily inform a user when target information of a current time point is transferred to the underwater moving object. CONSTITUTION: An underwater moving object information processor(100) processes information of an underwater moving object at the current time point according to the drive of the underwater moving object. A target information generator(200) generates information of a target at the current time point. An information estimator(300) produces the past time point when target noise received in the underwater moving object is emitted by using the information of the target and the underwater moving object at the current time point. The information estimator estimates target information at the past time point by using the information of the target and the underwater moving object at the current time point.,METHOD FOR ESTIMATING PASSIVE SONAR DATA OF UNDERWATER VEHICLE FOR REAL-TIME SIMULATION AND SIMULATING APPARATUS HAVING THE SAME,,,,
97469417,block6,2025,CN,"Flexible riser joint auxiliary device for offshore oil and gas, annulus operation system and operation method of annulus operation system","The invention belongs to the technical field of offshore oil and gas exploitation equipment, particularly relates to a flexible riser joint auxiliary device for offshore oil and gas, an annulus operation system and an operation method thereof, and is applied to an offshore oil and gas exploitation scene. The flexible riser joint auxiliary device for ocean oil and gas is provided with an underwater robot ROV operation auxiliary device, and the auxiliary device is communicated with an annular space in the joint body. The auxiliary device comprises an ROV normally-closed valve, a hydraulic pilot one-way valve and an ROV inserting hole, the underwater robot ROV achieves open-close control over the annulus by opening and closing the hydraulic pilot one-way valve and the ROV normally-closed valve, and therefore the underwater robot ROV can conveniently inject preservative liquid into the annulus from the flexible vertical pipe connector or sample and detect the annulus from the flexible vertical pipe connector. According to the method, the convenience and safety of maintenance operation of the flexible riser in the offshore oil and gas exploitation process are improved, and the reliability of annulus detection of the flexible riser is improved.","Flexible riser joint auxiliary device for offshore oil and gas, annulus operation system and operation method of annulus operation system",,,,
97608489,block6,2025,CN,Multi-scale marine benthos detection method based on global-local trans-attention fusion,"The invention discloses a multi-scale marine benthos detection method based on global-local cross-attention fusion, and the method comprises the steps: collecting and preprocessing submarine data information through an underwater robot, and building a multi-scale marine benthos data set; preprocessing the multi-scale marine benthic organism data set and dividing the multi-scale marine benthic organism data set into a training set and a test set; building a multi-scale benthic organism detection framework based on global-local cross-attention fusion; adopting the training set to train the multi-scale benthos detection framework to obtain a multi-scale marine benthos detection model; and performing deployment and hyper-parameter adjustment on the trained multi-scale marine benthos detection model, and using the obtained model to detect marine benthos. According to the method, histogram equalization is introduced to pre-process the image, so that the image contrast is effectively enhanced, and the problem of low contrast of the underwater image caused by uneven illumination, color degradation or blurring is solved.",Multi-scale marine benthos detection method based on global-local trans-attention fusion,,,,
56236627,block6,2014,CN,Underwater unmanned vehicle 4D synchronization deductive system,"The objective of the invention is to provide a deductive technology based on incomplete feedback information in the navigation process of an aircraft, the movement state of the aircraft may be visually observed, and the motion of the aircraft in the influence of the sea environment may be also visually observed. The underwater unmanned vehicle 4D synchronization deductive system is composed of three parts, namely a model simulation module, a visual simulation module and a simulation control part, each part has a simulation computer, and the communication among three computers is completed according to related protocols. Each part completes different simulation tasks to achieve the completion of real-time visual simulation. The mutual relation of the three different simulation computers is a motion control computer.",Underwater unmanned vehicle 4D synchronization deductive system,,,,
97328458,block6,2025,CN,Pipeline anti-corrosion layer detection method adopting dense interval potentiometry,"The invention provides a pipeline anti-corrosion layer detection method adopting a dense interval potential method, and relates to the field of pipeline anti-corrosion layer detection, which is characterized by comprising the following steps of: 1, setting a cathode protection system: for a pipeline adopting forced current potential cathode protection, before data acquisition, erecting satellite synchronous on-off devices at all constant potential positions for protecting the pipeline, and the satellite synchronization function is utilized to ensure accurate time control of the on-off device. The device and the method have the advantages that the millivolt-level signal acquisition effect of the potential of the anticorrosive coating is achieved by integrating the high-precision reference electrode array on the underwater detection platform, the millimeter-level positioning effect of the damaged point of the anticorrosive coating is achieved by adopting a 0.2-0.5 m dense interval potential gradient measurement method, and the detection accuracy is improved. Analyzing the potential abrupt change characteristic (delta Vgt; the effect of quantitatively evaluating the damage area and severity is achieved, and the effect of continuously and rapidly scanning a long-distance pipeline is achieved through autonomous cruise detection of the underwater robot.",Pipeline anti-corrosion layer detection method adopting dense interval potentiometry,,,,
